<<~ aka "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Not Walking Before Minting

Not Walking Before Minting names a concept derived at cost that the graph already held.

The node reasons a finding out from context — sometimes across several research waves — writes it as new, and only later discovers it standing in a meme nobody walked to. ''The graph knew; the reasoning never asked it.''

''Seven instances in one arc'': the constructor (`group-as-closure`, with the declaration built in) · anon-as-base and the one-way ratchet (`persona-circle`, better cited) · the commons-is-a-verb inversion (`cabal-realm`) · the word `realm` itself · the Shadowtalk UX seat (`dreamdeck-feed-architecture`) · the fractal shape (`multi-fractal`, `pattern-integrity = true`) · and fifteen cultural pattern-integrities sitting in a history bag with no edge from any api/pono meme.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ detect the moment a finding feels NEW — that feeling carries no evidence either way.
⏿ orient by ''walking the graph one hop'' from the nearest meme: read its edges, its residues, its history-bag neighbours.
◇ decide: found → cite it, and note whether the existing statement reads better (it commonly does).
▶ act — write the DELTA into the existing meme rather than a fresh meme beside it.
↺ if the graph held it, ask what ELSE sits one hop out; a rediscovery usually names a whole unwalked shelf.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

''Walk the edges before minting.''

The node MUST walk one hop from the nearest meme before seating a finding as new.
The node SHOULD read `role` and `register` before reading a body — the meta block answers //does this hold my thing// in one line.
The node MUST record a rediscovery when it happens, with the credit stated: //this already sits at X, better stated//, which reads as the most valuable finding a walk returns.

''What this failure actually costs'': not duplication — ''the reasoning''. A finding derived across three research waves and already held in canon spent those waves proving what one grep would have cited. And the graph's version usually carries a citation the derivation lacks.

''The deeper reading'': this names a RETRIEVAL failure, never a knowledge one. The house holds more than any one session can attend to, which is the sensorium's whole reason to exist — and until that instrument stands, walking is the manual form of it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/diagnostic>>

If a finding written as new already sits in a meme one hop from where the node was working, Not Walking Before Minting occurred.
If the walk ran and returned nothing, the mint stands earned.
If the graph's version reads WORSE than the derivation, that reads as a genuine refinement — write the delta into the existing meme, never a fresh one beside it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

